WEBVTT

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:07.380
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:14.540
The reading from the Sinhaxadeon for July 11 on which we commemorate our Holy Father

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:18.420
St. Sephroni of Essex.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:24.940
Our commandrite Sephroni Sakatov was born in Moscow in the year 1896.

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:30.740
He studied at the National School of Fine Arts in Moscow and took up painting as his career,

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:35.860
as well as endowing him richly with natural talents, God also gave him exceptional spiritual

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.460
gifts from the outset of his life.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:43.180
From a young age, he assimilated the spirit of the living God of his fathers.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:48.500
In his youth, he was possessed by a thirst for absolute being, and he devoted himself to

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:53.900
a serious consideration of the existential problems of his time and place.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:58.420
His intense metaphysical quest brought him to sense painfully the tragic character of

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.140
human existence.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:05.860
He came to belittle the idea that the absolute could be contained in the psychological level,

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:12.300
as he saw it, of the gospel commandments of love, and he strayed from the path of Christianity.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:17.300
He was attracted by the theories of Eastern religions, seeing in them a logical solution

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:22.700
to the grievous sight of suffering and pain, and he practiced for about eight years the

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:28.420
transcendental meditation that is linked to their psychological delusion of an impersonal

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:30.540
absolute.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:35.260
His return to Christianity was provoked by an awakening to the scriptural text of God's

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:40.340
revelation to Moses, I am that I am.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:46.100
By God's grace he understood that the absolute and unoriginant being is none other than the

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:53.380
personal God first revealed to Moses, the same God who has in these last days spoken to

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:58.140
us by his only begotten Son, by Jesus Christ.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:02.140
See Hebrews 1-2

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:06.900
From the moment of his personal meeting with him who is, Father Sephroni did not rest from

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:12.780
an intense striving to be initiated into the mystery of the God revealed to him, and to penetrate

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:18.940
the infinite dimensions of the person of Christ, in whose image man was created.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:24.740
With extremely intense mourning he lamented for decades his misguided quest for the impersonal,

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:28.860
imaginary, absolute of the oriental religions.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:35.620
He viewed his laps from Christianity as a fall like that of Adam and as a suicide on the metaphysical

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:37.180
plane.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:44.060
In his book we shall see him as he is, which is tantamount to his spiritual autobiography,

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:48.260
he describes how he lived out his repentance.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:54.660
In the year 1925, after a short period of studies at the St. Sirgeus Theological Institute,

00:02:54.660 --> 00:03:00.100
he left Paris for the Holy Mountain of Athos, where he lived for 22 years.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:06.780
He first settled in the monastery of St. Pantelemon, where he met and formed a close spiritual bond

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:12.980
with St. Syloan, 1866 through 1938.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:19.500
In whose person he saw clearly portrayed the authentic dimensions of Christian life.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:24.300
Father Sephirone had lived for about five years at St. Pantelemon's monastery, before he

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.820
met St. Syloan personally.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:32.380
He was ordained deacon in the year 1930, and each time he came out to the sanctuary to

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:38.620
sense the monks, he used to feel awe and shame when he passed in front of the saint.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:42.980
But he had not as yet had any occasion to speak with him.

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:49.140
A few years after his ordination to the deaconate, Father Sephirone was visited by a hermit, Father

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:54.300
Vladimir, and they spoke together on various spiritual matters.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:59.100
Father Vladimir was moved to compunction by their conversation, as well as by the spiritual

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:05.340
atmosphere of their whole meeting, and he spontaneously addressed Father Sephirone with the question,

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:09.300
Father Sephirone, how can someone be saved?

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:15.780
At that moment, Father Sephirone was preparing tea for Father Vladimir, and he replied,

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:22.780
stay on the verge of despair, but when you see that you are going to fall over, draw back,

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:27.540
and have a cup of tea, and he handed him some tea.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:32.820
This word, and above all the strong feeling which had transmitted, struck the hermit, and

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:34.900
he left shaken.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:39.820
He went afterwards to Saint Siloan to seek advice, and check the veracity of Father

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:42.540
Sephirone's exhortation.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:46.780
The next day, Father Sephirone was coming down the staircase from the main building of the

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:52.660
monastery, which had many stories, towards the central courtyard, and Saint Siloan was coming

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:55.500
up from the warehouse in the opposite direction.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:05:00.380
They would normally have met outside the entrance to the main church, but Father Sephirone,

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:05.980
that of his habitual respect, moved aside to avoid getting in the way of the holy man.

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:11.980
Saint Siloan, however, also changed direction, so that they met unavoidably in front of

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:13.820
the re-fectory.

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:18.540
At that point, Saint Siloan asked Father Sephirone.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:24.740
Father Sephirone did Father Vladimir visit you yesterday, and Father Sephirone, omitting all

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:32.180
the intermediate stages usual in conversation, replied by asking, did I make any mistake?

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:38.740
Likewise, going straight to the point, Saint Siloan said to him, no, but what you said was

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:40.820
beyond his measure.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:46.300
If you like, come and see me tomorrow, and we can speak more about this.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:52.180
Thus, Father Sephirone visited Saint Siloan, who told him about his own life.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:57.300
He recounted the fifteen-year-long battle he had waged against evil spirits.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:04.140
He confided to him the revelatory word of Christ, keep thy mind in hell, and despair not,

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:08.900
which marked a crucial moment in his spiritual struggle, and which was powerful enough to

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:14.740
save him from every diabolic temptation and purify him from proud thoughts.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:20.060
This historic meeting had a definitive effect on Father Sephirone's later spiritual evolution

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:22.460
and on his theology.

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:27.460
His communications with Saint Siloan reassured Father Sephirone that he was not misguided

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:31.540
in the spirit of repentance, which perpetually inflamed him.

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:36.300
He was instructed by the saint's teaching, and because of his unwavering faith in the

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:42.900
Stuttites' word, he acquired stability in his ascetic life and was led to freedom from passions.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:47.540
He lived out the rest of his days, both in the desert, and later in his service in the

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:53.060
world, testifying to the fact that only by voluntarily descending to hell, following

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:58.820
the pattern set by the gospel, can the believer be placed securely on the path of God and

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:05.500
learn the indescribable humility of Christ and be united with him.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:10.460
Father Sephirone held Stuttites' Siloan in such respect and trust that in spirit he

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:12.940
venerated his very footsteps.

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:17.820
He spoke and wrote about how he considered his close contact with St. Siloan as God's

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:19.860
greatest gift to him.

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:24.900
He remained close to him until the end of the saint's life, and then, with the blessing

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:29.820
of his abbot and the counsel of elders of the monastery, he withdrew to the desert of

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:31.820
Mount Athos.

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:37.780
From his hermit's cell, he served as Father Confessor to the monasteries of Saint Paul, Gregorio,

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:44.020
Simonas Petras, Xenofontos, and to many skitties and other groups of monks.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:50.940
In the year 1947, he left Athos to return to France, and in the year 1948, he published

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:56.780
in Russian the manuscripts entrusted to him by St. Siloan before his death, having added

00:07:56.780 --> 00:08:03.100
some biographical information and an extensive analysis of the saint's teaching.

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:09.860
In the year 1959, he founded in Essex, England, the community which was to become the patriarchal

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:17.260
St. Pagic monastery of Saint John the Baptist, where he fell asleep in the Lord on July 11,

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:20.380
in the year 1993.

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:26.180
In spiritual terms, Father Sephroni stands out as a sign from God for his generation.

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:31.380
He lived out the tragedy, the anxieties, the difficulties, and the quests of the much

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:37.820
troubled twentieth century, and through his living example, his prayer, and his word,

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:42.140
he gave answers to the burning questions of his contemporaries.

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:47.580
Father Sephroni's laps in his youth into the impersonal theology of the Oriental religions

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:52.900
was transformed by the wondrous providence of God into a gift from heaven.

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:57.700
Although Father Sephroni had never consciously rejected Christ, he nonetheless considered

00:08:57.700 --> 00:09:04.580
his going astray as apostasy and as a crime against the love of the God of his fathers.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:09.900
This became the starting point of his unremitting deep, inconsolable repentance.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:15.300
Through the grace given despair of repentance, as he himself describes it, he was liberated

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:21.900
from the bonds of the old man, see Ephesians 4, 22, et al.

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:27.780
He was unable to contemplate without passions the uncreated light of the face of Christ.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:34.380
From then on, he understood the spiritual place of the human person in its divine human fullness.

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:40.540
He saw the two great commandments of love become the law of his whole being, the first shown

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:47.580
in an insatiable desire for God, and the second in prayer for the world to the point of self-forgetting

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:49.580
and abundant tears.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:55.500
In such agonized prayer, he spent himself for decades.

00:09:55.500 --> 00:10:00.700
Because Father Sephroni had the grace given experience unique to Christianity of the personal

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:06.900
or, as he preferred to say, hypostatic principle, as well as knowing from within the context

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:13.140
of the Indian religions, he proved an invaluable apologist for orthodox Hesicastic practice

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:17.500
in a challenging epoch whose spirit is syncretistic.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:21.740
With persuasive and compelling authority, he succeeded in describing the difference between

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:28.860
the two ascetic theories, Oriental and Christian, which are as far apart as the uncreated is from

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:30.500
the created.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:36.900
He contrasted the spiritual suicide to which transcendental meditation leads with the incomparable

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:43.780
life-giving experience of meeting and being united with the personal God of Scripture.

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:47.820
Oriental Sephroni was endowed with many gifts of the Holy Spirit.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:52.780
The most impressive was the living Word of God which he grasped through prayer and carried

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:54.380
in his heart.

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:56.660
He was a man of the Word.

00:10:56.660 --> 00:11:02.020
Every contact with him was an opening to new understanding in life, and even his most

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:06.180
everyday words conveyed grace to those who turned to him.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:11.860
He prayed continuously and intensely for those who suffer and rejoiced more than over any

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:18.100
miraculous occurrences to see his Word and his prayer transform their hearts.

00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:23.900
He struggled to diminish their pain, but above all he spent himself to his utmost in the service

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:30.380
of the greatest and most significant miracle of our temporal life, the union of human beings

00:11:30.380 --> 00:11:34.620
with the spirit of the living and eternal God.

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:39.660
No phenomenon in the spiritual life could take him by surprise.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:42.020
He had traced the whole path.

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:47.380
At one and the same time, both unfathomable depths and immeasurable heights were within

00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:48.900
his reach.

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:54.460
As well as knowing the grace of repentance, he was familiar with the alternations that occur

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:57.060
in the practice of inner prayer.

00:11:57.060 --> 00:12:02.340
He was schooled in the regenerating Word of Christ and had taken upon himself his martyric

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:03.660
priesthood.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:09.420
He deeply loved the divine liturgy and affirmed that to celebrate it appropriately is a spiritually

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:13.700
fruitful prayer as his hecasm in the desert.

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:19.180
He used to say, to be a Christian, one must be like an artist.

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:24.260
Just as artists are captivated by the subjects they paint and by the desire to portray them

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:31.300
as perfectly as possible, so too the Christian is captivated by Christ and by a desire to attain

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:33.660
to his endless perfection.

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:44.200
I press on to make it my own because Christ Jesus has made me his own Philippians 3-12.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:50.300
When Father Sephroni felt his end approaching, he said, I have said everything to God.

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:52.900
I have finished what I had to do.

00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:55.260
Now I must depart.

00:12:55.260 --> 00:13:00.740
He summoned the members of the community one by one, imparting to each his final instructions

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:03.420
and a personal farewell word.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:09.540
Then with humility as well as boldness, he wrote a fervent letter to his all holiness, patriarch

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:14.540
Bartholomew, with heartfelt thanks for all the care shown towards his monastery.

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:19.340
As well as expressing deep gratitude, he begged the patriarch to defend the fragile work of

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:21.060
his hands.

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:28.660
Give your blessing upon the lowly sheep of my fold that this place, small, poor and insignificant,

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:36.020
founded upon many tears and heartfelt groaning and blood and sweat may never be forsaken

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:39.620
by your affectionate care and good pleasure.

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:44.580
He ended the letter by asking his hierarchy's blessing to depart to the longed-for light

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:46.980
of the risen Christ.

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:52.220
Father Sephroni passed away peacefully and now reposes in the Lord, but he continues through

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:58.300
his word and his prayers to minister for the miracle that his soul desired, the regeneration

00:13:58.300 --> 00:14:04.860
of the faithful and their entrance richly provided for into the eternal kingdom of our Lord

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:12.380
and Savior, Jesus Christ, 2 Peter 1-11.

00:14:12.380 --> 00:14:18.380
In all his books, he develops Christian anthropology in the light of St. Syloon's experience, which

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:25.180
he also shared, in his teaching on the person he continually portrays St. Syloon as a model.

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:29.660
His anthropology follows the tradition of the Church, but he develops it with a particular

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:35.820
emphasis and an original robustness and inspiration, which grew out of his long and exceptional

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:39.540
trials in the furnace of God's training.

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:44.780
The originality of Father Sephroni's theology lies in his interpretation of certain aspects

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:50.300
of Christian revelation in such a way as to answer satisfactorily the theological problems

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:51.700
of his time.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:56.940
The central axis of his living theology is his deep investigation into the meaning of the

00:14:56.940 --> 00:15:03.540
personal or hypostatic principle in divine being and in humanity, and his description

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:09.740
of certain features of humanity which determine man's final realization as far as this is possible

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:12.860
within the limits of earthly life.

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:18.420
This theology is presented as an account of man's personal encounter with the living God,

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:23.060
and as a chronicle of the experience of divine light.

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:28.980
St. Syloon and his disciple and biographer Archimandrite Sephroni deserve a place in the history

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:30.740
of the Church.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:36.660
St. Syloon and Archimandrite Sephroni are a subject worthy of consideration in the academic

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:39.580
circles of contemporary theology.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:45.740
Their uniqueness of Orthodox anthropology has the last word to say in response to the challenges

00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:50.260
and existential problems of our generation.

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:56.220
Through the prayers of our Holy Father's, O Lord Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.780
and save us.

00:15:58.780 --> 00:16:03.420
The following works of Father Sephroni have been published in English.

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:10.980
St. Syloon the Athenite, St. Peter's monastery of St. John the Baptist, 1991, Christwood, St.

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:20.900
Vladimir's seminary press, 1999, his life is mine, St. Vladimir's seminary press, 1977.

00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:28.660
We shall see him as he is, St. Peter's monastery of St. John the Baptist, 1988.

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:36.500
On prayer, St. Peter's monastery of St. John the Baptist, 1996, Christwood, St. Vladimir's

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:40.180
seminary press, 1998.

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:47.980
Words of life, St. Peter's monastery of St. John the Baptist, 1988, Principles of Orthodox

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:54.540
monasticism in the Orthodox Ethos, extracts from St. Syloon the Athenite are published

00:16:54.540 --> 00:17:03.340
as The Monk of Mount Athos, St. Ed's Syloon, 1866 through 1938, St. Vladimir's seminary

00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:09.580
press, 1975, wisdom from Mount Athos, writings of St. Syloon.
